Real-time planning: pinning visits

Real-time planning can be disruptive to technician’s schedules. Real-time planning is also not always possible, for instance:

Customers might only be available to provide access to the property at certain times, and the visit can only be completed during a specific time window.

A technician might already have the equipment or materials loaded for a specific visit and is unable to complete visits other than those they are currently assigned.

Visits that have already been assigned and scheduled can be pinned to prevent them from being rescheduled.

There are two types of pinning.

Block pinning:

Block pinning involves pinning a continuous block of visits from the start of the shift. This approach maintains the order and timing of the scheduled visits.

Pinning individual visits:

Pinning individual visits is more targeted than block pinning and specifies individual visits to pin. This approach makes it possible to add new visits, or reschedule existing visits before the pinned visit.

This guide explains pinning with the following examples:

1. Block pinning with freezeTime
2. Block pinning whole vehicle shifts
3. Block pinning partial vehicle shifts
4. Pinning individual visits
1. Block pinning with freezeTime
LEARN HOW TO CONFIGURE AN API KEY TO RUN THE EXAMPLES IN THIS GUIDE:

In the Real-time planning: emergency visit example, Ann had three visits scheduled for the day, while Beth had one. An emergency visit, Visit M, needed to be added to the schedule. The emergency visit was close to Ann’s existing route, and so the real-time plan reassigned Ann’s final visit of the day, Visit E, to Beth, and Ann was assigned the emergency Visit M.

However, this may not always be the best solution.

If Ann already has the material for Visit E loaded in her van, the visit cannot be assigned to another technician.

In this case, Visit E can be pinned so that it remains assigned to Ann, and the emergency visit, Visit M, will be assigned to Beth.

Real-time planning pins all visits before freezeTime, including visits that technicians are already traveling to. Pinning additional visits gives you greater control over blocks of specific visits after the time specified in freezeTime.

If there were additional visits between freezeTime and Visit E in Ann’s shift itinerary, those visits would also need to be pinned.
